Jonadab the Unsightly One wrote:
> Janis Papanagnou <janis_papanag...@hotmail.com> wrote:
>
>> He will teleport to the upstairs (not to the downstairs), so if you
>> cover the upstairs you have all the time you need to kill him.
>
> But when I get close to killing him he leaves and escapes down.
> That has happened to me in every game so far where I survived
> long enough to make it into Gehennom (which, admittedly, is not
> very many games yet; I usually die before Delphi).

You've been walking near the down stairs or holes in the floor.  Major
demons will teleport to the up stairs not to the down staris when
injured.  His level is no teleport so all you need to do is stay well
away from either down stairs or holes, walk steadily towards the up
stairs, battle him every time he appears.  Eventually you either kill
him with a lucky high damage shot or beat him to the upstairs and kill
him there.  If he beats you to the up stairs he'll flee up so chase him.
But once up you're on a teleport allowed level so don't hit him. 
Teleport directly to the up stairs.  He'll chase you there but since you
did not hit him you'll beazt him there.  Then kill him there.  He won't
leave because the only stairs close by are the up stairs.

He'll escape either up or down but he'll always go to the up stairs to
heal never to the down stairs.  You have not been using that second fact
against him.

If you have a very high damage weapon it can easily happen that you will
kill him with a single shot while you are walking towards the up stairs.
Playing combat wombat characters that's happened to me as many times as
chasing him up once.  Grayswindir rules for a reason.  As does magic
missile spell or whatever he's not immune to.


